  "file": "src/router/providers.ts",
  "A": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "An operator switches a provider to unlimited after a utilization warning has been saved. The dashboard continues showing that warning, indefinitely when it has no reset time, even though the provider is available.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun \"$TMPDIR/quota-adjudication-045.ts\"",
    "output": "C1 before switch: [{\"provider\":\"work\",\"window\":\"five_hour\",\"utilization\":0.99,\"resetsAt\":null,\"severity\":\"exhausted\",\"routing\":\"Router skips this provider; no eligible fallback providers are known.\",\"createdAt\":1000000}]\nC1 after switch + low reading + ten years: {\"state\":\"ok\",\"headroom\":1,\"alerts\":[{\"provider\":\"work\",\"window\":\"five_hour\",\"utilization\":0.99,\"resetsAt\":null,\"severity\":\"exhausted\",\"routing\":\"eligible\",\"createdAt\":1000000}]}"
   },
   "evidence": "The throwaway script created a window alert, reconstructed the tracker with quota=\"unlimited\" using the same store, observed utilization 0.01, advanced the clock ten years, and refreshed alerts. HEAD returns at `if (p.def.billing !== \"subscription\" || p.def.quota === \"unlimited\") return;` before clearing window alerts. `refreshAlerts()` only expires alerts and updates routing descriptions; null-reset alerts never expire. Base had only the billing condition and no unlimited mode."
  },
  "B": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "Someone whose Claude provider already raised a 99% 'exhausted' quota alert switches it to quota = \"unlimited\" and restarts. The provider now reports headroom 1 and state ok, but the old 'exhausted' alert stays in the alerts list and UI, and never goes away if the window had no reset time.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun $TMPDIR/c1.ts  (step 1: windows-mode tracker observes seven_day utilization .99 with resetsAt null; step 2: new tracker on the same store with quota unlimited, setRoutingDescription, observeWindows .5; step 3: list alerts)",
    "output": "before: [[\"claude\",\"seven_day\",\"exhausted\"]]\nheadroom: 1 state: ok\nafter unlimited: [[\"claude\",\"seven_day\",\"exhausted\",0.99]]"
   },
   "evidence": "providers.ts:574 `if (p.def.billing !== \"subscription\" || p.def.quota === \"unlimited\") return;` returns before any clearAlert call. refreshAlerts (273-280) only calls expireAlerts (which uses the reset time) and rewrites the routing text, so a persisted alert for an unlimited provider is never purged. Alerts are only read by /api/alerts (http.ts:545) and the hard_limit lookup in record(), so routing is unaffected and the effect is display-only."
  }
