  "file": "src/router/config-catalog.ts",
  "A": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "A user upgrades and runs `limitless providers export --write`, as the deprecation notice tells them to. Every provider in their config now carries quota = \"windows\" even though they never chose a quota setting. If they roll back to the previous release, it rejects the config with 'unknown fields quota' and the daemon will not start.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun $TMPDIR/c2.ts ; bun $TMPDIR/c2b.ts  (export the default catalog at head, then feed the TOML to the base commit's resolveCatalog)",
    "output": "7 quota lines\n[[providers]] id = \"claude\" ... billing = \"subscription\"\nquota = \"windows\"\n...\nbase rejects: providers[0]: unknown fields quota"
   },
   "evidence": "config-catalog.ts:60 `quota: quota.default(\"windows\")`. Lines 126-129 stamp `quota: p.quota ?? \"windows\"` on every built-in provider, and line 149 does the same for legacy tables. providerFields() therefore exports quota for every provider. Base providerSchema is a z.strictObject without quota, and base config.ts:158 calls resolveCatalog(raw.providers) while loading config, so the exported file fails to load on base. The test change `PROVIDERS.map((p) => ({ ...p, quota: \"windows\" }))` confirms the default is always stamped on."
  },
  "B": {
   "verdict": "NOT_REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "Exported configuration explicitly includes the default quota mode; no incorrect behavior was demonstrated.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun -e 'import {isDeepStrictEqual} from \"node:util\"; import {resolveCatalog,exportProviders} from \"./src/router/config-catalog.ts\"; const c=resolveCatalog(); const r=resolveCatalog(Bun.TOML.parse(exportProviders(c)).providers); console.log(JSON.stringify({providers:c.providers.length, windowsAssignments:exportProviders(c).match(/^quota = \"windows\"$/gm)?.length,providersRoundTrip:isDeepStrictEqual(c.providers,r.providers), modelsRoundTrip:isDeepStrictEqual(c.models,r.models)}));'",
    "output": "{\"providers\":7,\"windowsAssignments\":7,\"providersRoundTrip\":true,\"modelsRoundTrip\":true}"
   },
   "evidence": "HEAD adds `quota: quota.default(\"windows\")` and normalizes built-ins with `quota: p.quota ?? \"windows\"`. The existing exporter serializes complete provider definitions through `assignments(providerFields(p))`, including other default-valued fields. Base lacked the quota field. Explicitly exporting this valid default preserves provider and model definitions on reload; no requirement says defaults must be omitted."
  }
